# Shell scripts must keep LF endings, whatever the machine that commits them.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where git's autocrlf happily rewrites a
# checked-out file to CRLF. A shell script that reaches a Linux container with
# CRLF endings fails on its first line: the kernel reads the shebang as
# "/bin/sh\r", finds no such interpreter, and the container dies with
# "no such file or directory" — naming a file that is plainly right there.
#
# The Dockerfile's entrypoint is exactly that script, so this is not theoretical.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
